WEBVTT

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:25.451
Support Admin Watch on
kissasia.cam or kisskh.org

00:00:27.590 --> 00:00:31.469
LAST
SUMMER

00:00:33.263 --> 00:00:36.599
This is going to be our home now.
Look. What do you think?

00:00:36.683 --> 00:00:39.811
Eighty percent of my insomnia
started at this Peanut House.

00:00:39.894 --> 00:00:41.563
Should we go in? Let's check it out.

00:00:41.646 --> 00:00:43.940
Which side is our home?

00:00:44.023 --> 00:00:45.817
Which side do you want it to be?

00:00:48.695 --> 00:00:52.115
If I wanted to cry…
No, let me correct that.

00:00:52.907 --> 00:00:55.618
When my hands got cold, I studied…

00:00:56.619 --> 00:01:00.957
thinking, "If I became the top student,
got a perfect score, and I did my part…

00:01:02.250 --> 00:01:03.918
my hands would feel less cold."

00:01:04.002 --> 00:01:05.336
Mom!

00:01:05.420 --> 00:01:06.963
-Ha-gyeong!
-Let's play!

00:01:07.046 --> 00:01:08.298
I don't want to eat!

00:01:10.967 --> 00:01:13.094
Don't be so difficult. Just eat!

00:01:14.053 --> 00:01:15.638
Stop that. Move.

00:01:18.391 --> 00:01:19.851
REPORT CARD
CLASS RANK 1

00:01:21.352 --> 00:01:22.353
I'll leave.

00:01:23.396 --> 00:01:26.316
Mom, I'm just gonna leave this house!

00:01:29.110 --> 00:01:29.944
Ha-gyeong!

00:01:37.118 --> 00:01:39.913
I'm not even second or third place.

00:01:41.789 --> 00:01:44.167
Do I even have a place in this house?

00:01:45.460 --> 00:01:48.588
Baek Do-ha said
that a home is where people live.

00:01:50.798 --> 00:01:53.468
That's only knowing half the story.

00:01:53.551 --> 00:01:54.385
This animal…

00:01:54.469 --> 00:01:56.095
'Cause there are many people here.

00:01:56.179 --> 00:01:57.347
…has a pocket.

00:01:57.430 --> 00:02:00.516
Even in the hot summer,
my hands were always cold.

00:02:05.605 --> 00:02:07.732
The foster siblings
who passed through our home…

00:02:07.815 --> 00:02:08.733
Bye, Ha-gyeong.

00:02:09.776 --> 00:02:10.693
I'm leaving.

00:02:15.949 --> 00:02:17.116
…and Baek Do-young…

00:02:19.994 --> 00:02:21.329
and Dad…

00:02:24.791 --> 00:02:26.042
I'm heading off.

00:02:27.085 --> 00:02:28.127
…and Mom…

00:02:30.338 --> 00:02:31.631
and Baek Do-ha.

00:02:33.591 --> 00:02:36.761
They kept coming…

00:02:38.346 --> 00:02:39.722
and going.

00:02:51.150 --> 00:02:52.068
Hey, Su-bak.

00:02:53.152 --> 00:02:56.823
And finally,
I was left all alone in the house…

00:03:00.910 --> 00:03:02.286
and he came back.

00:03:03.621 --> 00:03:04.497
You came back.

00:03:34.027 --> 00:03:36.321
-Good morning.
-Good morning.

00:03:46.706 --> 00:03:50.043
JONG-MAN JR.

00:04:03.389 --> 00:04:05.016
That's right. Hi, Su-bak.

00:04:11.981 --> 00:04:14.192
-Did you sleep well?
-Yes, totally.

00:04:18.321 --> 00:04:19.947
So you went for a run.

00:04:20.031 --> 00:04:21.699
You should pace yourself well.

00:04:22.992 --> 00:04:25.203
Living with you
takes stamina and mental strength.

00:04:26.871 --> 00:04:27.705
Why?

00:04:28.664 --> 00:04:29.957
Good morning.

00:05:03.866 --> 00:05:07.286
-You seem really happy.
-Yes, I'm super happy.

00:05:13.376 --> 00:05:14.836
You two really live together.

00:05:18.714 --> 00:05:21.217
-Good morning.
-Morning.

00:05:21.300 --> 00:05:24.470
It's really nice to see, right? Nice.

00:05:24.554 --> 00:05:28.307
In this era of low birth rates,
having more young people in our village

00:05:28.391 --> 00:05:30.351
is a really good thing.

00:05:30.435 --> 00:05:31.978
It is good, indeed.

00:05:32.061 --> 00:05:35.231
Will Patan-myeon's average age
go down now?

00:05:37.525 --> 00:05:40.778
At least that sign was made properly.

00:05:40.862 --> 00:05:44.157
Thanks to that,
Dr. Song's house looks pretty decent now.

00:05:45.116 --> 00:05:48.244
The past few days of construction,

00:05:48.327 --> 00:05:51.038
your neighbors have been
putting up with all the noise.

00:05:51.122 --> 00:05:53.291
Why don't you go over and say hi sometime?

00:05:53.374 --> 00:05:54.208
Great idea.

00:05:54.292 --> 00:05:55.501
-Of course.
-Right.

00:05:55.585 --> 00:05:57.378
Do you have any dugyeonju left?

00:05:58.296 --> 00:06:00.423
-No.
-No, we don't.

00:06:01.340 --> 00:06:02.466
Why?

00:06:03.342 --> 00:06:05.803
I'll be late for work. I've got to go.
Have a good day.

00:06:05.887 --> 00:06:07.054
-Sure.
-Okay.

00:06:07.138 --> 00:06:09.056
-You're not coming in my car?
-No.

00:06:09.640 --> 00:06:11.392
But you can't say hi without dugyeonju.

00:06:12.226 --> 00:06:14.937
We actually broke two bottles of it.

00:06:15.021 --> 00:06:16.731
You broke those?

00:06:17.648 --> 00:06:19.275
-You want it?
-Of course.

00:06:19.358 --> 00:06:21.068
Then we'll buy you each a bottle.

00:06:21.152 --> 00:06:22.987
-Good.
-Special edition, right?

00:06:23.112 --> 00:06:24.989
PACHEON CITY HALL
WHERE NATURE BREATHES

00:06:26.324 --> 00:06:28.784
-What do I do about this?
-What?

00:06:29.327 --> 00:06:32.872
He says the observatory project
destroyed his family.

00:06:32.955 --> 00:06:34.290
Destroyed how?

00:06:36.417 --> 00:06:38.502
"This rural village is already dark.

00:06:38.586 --> 00:06:41.589
Is it right to leave only
darker matters behind?

00:06:41.672 --> 00:06:43.216
Correct this now or I'll…

00:06:43.841 --> 00:06:47.261
split your head in two with a crowbar…"
What do I do?

00:06:47.345 --> 00:06:49.513
People like that probably won't show up.

00:06:50.139 --> 00:06:53.851
-Officer Song, come to my desk.
-Yes, ma'am.

00:06:55.895 --> 00:06:56.729
Yes.

00:06:57.355 --> 00:06:59.815
Please hurry with the detailed plan
for Patan High

00:06:59.899 --> 00:07:01.317
and share it with Pluto.

00:07:01.400 --> 00:07:03.819
-Maybe by this week--
-I've sent it already.

00:07:04.487 --> 00:07:05.321
Already?

00:07:05.404 --> 00:07:08.491
And if you approve the material cost
by 1:00 p.m.,

00:07:08.574 --> 00:07:10.243
I'll place the order right away.

00:07:10.326 --> 00:07:12.286
Why are you placing the order so soon?

00:07:12.370 --> 00:07:14.121
Don't we have enough time?

00:07:14.789 --> 00:07:17.750
Now, Pluto checks
the ordered materials themselves too.

00:07:18.960 --> 00:07:23.089
To meet the deadline, August 31st,
there can't be a single error.

00:07:23.172 --> 00:07:26.092
Wait, August 31?

00:07:26.592 --> 00:07:28.010
You're going overboard again.

00:07:28.594 --> 00:07:29.971
Pluto won't allow that.

00:07:31.681 --> 00:07:35.935
Director Baek Do-ha set the date himself.

00:07:36.018 --> 00:07:38.020
PATAN HIGH OBSERVATORY RENOVATION

00:07:39.564 --> 00:07:41.148
AUGUST 31 - COMPLETION

00:07:41.232 --> 00:07:43.568
You all saw the schedule I sent, right?

00:07:44.110 --> 00:07:45.027
-Yes.
-Yes.

00:07:45.111 --> 00:07:46.237
This renovation project

00:07:46.320 --> 00:07:49.156
has far more invisible problems
than visible ones.

00:07:49.782 --> 00:07:53.494
So I organized and checked
potential issues that may occur on-site,

00:07:53.578 --> 00:07:54.954
so review them carefully.

00:07:55.037 --> 00:07:58.249
Why are you even checking
fine dust levels?

00:07:58.332 --> 00:08:00.084
To start the interior work.

00:08:00.167 --> 00:08:02.795
Taking care of workers' conditions
improves efficiency.

00:08:04.797 --> 00:08:07.466
The completion date
can't be delayed even by one day.

00:08:07.550 --> 00:08:10.052
That's not an option for us.
To achieve that,

00:08:10.136 --> 00:08:13.014
we'll finish demolition and repairs
by the end of this month,

00:08:13.097 --> 00:08:15.182
exterior finishing by mid-July,

00:08:15.266 --> 00:08:18.603
and interior work by early August.

00:08:18.686 --> 00:08:19.604
Then…

00:08:19.687 --> 00:08:20.688
OFFICIAL COMPLETION

00:08:22.023 --> 00:08:23.232
Done.

00:08:24.191 --> 00:08:26.527
There's no time to waste.

00:08:35.369 --> 00:08:37.288
Officer Song's hazing is over.

00:08:39.081 --> 00:08:41.250
She even sent the detailed plan.

00:08:41.334 --> 00:08:44.462
Looks like she's ready
to fully support our project now.

00:08:45.588 --> 00:08:48.049
But why did she suddenly
change her mind overnight?

00:08:49.175 --> 00:08:50.593
Who knows.

00:08:50.676 --> 00:08:52.261
Season Two really started.

00:08:54.639 --> 00:08:57.391
I told Yu-jeong
and cleared my whole week.

00:08:58.267 --> 00:09:00.019
-Starting today, I can work until--
-No.

00:09:00.936 --> 00:09:02.063
I'll leave on time.

00:09:03.147 --> 00:09:06.275
I hate working overtime,
so I put my soul into the planning.

00:09:07.943 --> 00:09:10.279
-Just today?
-No, every day.

00:09:10.863 --> 00:09:11.822
Every day?

00:09:43.479 --> 00:09:45.564
Oh, my! You scared me.

00:09:46.816 --> 00:09:49.735
Why are you sprawled out in my house?

00:09:49.819 --> 00:09:52.446
Su-bak's treats are all here.

00:09:54.657 --> 00:09:57.368
Could you not just
waltz in and out of my place?

00:09:57.451 --> 00:09:59.161
And you can't feed him
just anything.

00:10:01.997 --> 00:10:02.873
Jeez.

00:10:14.135 --> 00:10:16.762
I couldn't get the portion quite right.

00:10:17.930 --> 00:10:21.350
Like you said, it's hard
to deal with food waste in this house.

00:10:21.434 --> 00:10:23.102
Sharing food with your neighbor helps.

00:10:31.152 --> 00:10:34.155
Living with you
is making me talk just like you.

00:10:35.740 --> 00:10:38.200
"I made it for you."
That's all I needed to say.

00:11:00.181 --> 00:11:01.015
Sit.

00:11:37.676 --> 00:11:38.677
What now?

00:11:39.428 --> 00:11:41.847
Can we talk after you're done eating?

00:11:50.439 --> 00:11:51.607
COHABITATION AGREEMENT

00:12:04.870 --> 00:12:08.374
"Until August 31st, no matter
what unexpected situation arises,

00:12:08.457 --> 00:12:10.668
Baek Do-ha and Song Ha-gyeong
will live together.

00:12:11.210 --> 00:12:12.503
If this clause is violated,

00:12:12.586 --> 00:12:15.589
Song Ha-gyeong transfers 100%
of Peanut House to Baek Do-ha."

00:12:15.673 --> 00:12:18.175
-What's this?
-A cohabitation agreement.

00:12:19.260 --> 00:12:23.430
For our comfortable and safe cohabitation,

00:12:23.514 --> 00:12:25.683
I think we need a clear arrangement.

00:12:26.600 --> 00:12:28.561
There's no guarantee
you won't run away again.

00:12:28.644 --> 00:12:29.728
Run away?

00:12:31.063 --> 00:12:35.734
Think about what you did to me
before we ended up living together here.

00:12:35.818 --> 00:12:37.319
You sued me out of the blue,

00:12:37.403 --> 00:12:40.948
then dropped the lawsuit
saying you'd give up ownership.

00:12:41.031 --> 00:12:43.450
And now,
you want to try living together.

00:12:43.534 --> 00:12:46.453
What if something comes up
between us again

00:12:46.537 --> 00:12:48.247
while we're living together?

00:12:48.330 --> 00:12:49.498
Something like what?

00:12:49.582 --> 00:12:53.419
You leaving the house again
or disappearing from my life,

00:12:53.502 --> 00:12:55.546
or me receiving a second complaint.

00:12:55.629 --> 00:12:58.257
I need to prepare
for all those scenarios.

00:12:58.882 --> 00:13:01.135
Our summers always had
a lot of unexpected things.

00:13:02.511 --> 00:13:03.429
I don't trust you.

00:13:21.447 --> 00:13:24.950
"Detailed contract for shared living
at the Peanut House.

00:13:26.410 --> 00:13:30.080
If the original term of the contract,
the completion date, isn't fulfilled,

00:13:30.164 --> 00:13:32.458
the ownership of the house
shall be fully transferred

00:13:32.541 --> 00:13:34.251
to Party A, Song Ha-gyeong."

00:13:34.335 --> 00:13:37.921
I revised it to contract format
with detailed clauses.

00:13:40.507 --> 00:13:44.094
Starting today, electricity, water, gas,
and maintenance fees will be split evenly.

00:13:44.178 --> 00:13:46.764
Shared spaces can be used
only during designated time slots.

00:13:46.847 --> 00:13:48.599
And let's not enter each other's spaces.

00:13:49.266 --> 00:13:52.227
You can't just come and go as you please.

00:13:53.395 --> 00:13:54.647
And most importantly,

00:13:54.730 --> 00:13:57.691
the premise is that
we do our work professionally.

00:13:57.775 --> 00:14:00.611
Let's keep the private
and professional parts separate

00:14:00.694 --> 00:14:03.614
and respect each other's spaces
at all times. Got it?

00:14:03.697 --> 00:14:05.366
So you'll respect my space too.

00:14:05.449 --> 00:14:06.659
Isn't that obvious?

00:14:07.660 --> 00:14:10.454
Hey… I have one question.

00:14:13.123 --> 00:14:15.125
What changed your mind
about living with me?

00:14:16.418 --> 00:14:17.378
Can I ask what it is?

00:14:19.838 --> 00:14:21.298
To shatter your fantasy.

00:14:22.841 --> 00:14:25.010
I thought about it, and you were right.

00:14:25.844 --> 00:14:28.722
We need to live together
for this to really end.

00:14:31.141 --> 00:14:33.185
You have too many fantasies
about this house.

00:14:33.769 --> 00:14:37.064
It's just a house, but you have fantasies
because you haven't lived here.

00:14:37.648 --> 00:14:39.900
Break them while living here.

00:14:41.527 --> 00:14:43.779
Right. I have a question too.

00:14:48.409 --> 00:14:49.618
Since yesterday, this part…

00:14:52.371 --> 00:14:54.415
"No matter
what unexpected situation arises."

00:14:54.498 --> 00:14:56.000
It's really been bothering me.

00:14:57.292 --> 00:14:58.502
What unexpected situation?

00:15:08.012 --> 00:15:09.722
It's called "unexpected" for a reason.

00:15:10.264 --> 00:15:12.474
Only an idiot
would give a heads-up about it.

00:15:16.395 --> 00:15:18.897
Anyway, got it.

00:15:37.791 --> 00:15:38.667
RECIPIENT BAEK DO-HA

00:15:40.836 --> 00:15:41.920
Who is it?

00:15:42.838 --> 00:15:43.797
RECIPIENT BAEK DO-HA

00:15:46.967 --> 00:15:47.926
RECIPIENT BAEK DO-HA

00:15:50.137 --> 00:15:51.055
RECIPIENT BAEK DO-HA

00:15:55.642 --> 00:15:56.810
He's unbelievable.

00:15:59.980 --> 00:16:01.273
Where did he go?

00:16:01.356 --> 00:16:02.191
BAEK DO-HA

00:16:04.777 --> 00:16:06.070
-Hey, Song.
-Are you crazy?

00:16:06.612 --> 00:16:08.489
How many packages did you order?

00:16:08.572 --> 00:16:11.116
And why do you keep
sending your stuff to my house?

00:16:11.200 --> 00:16:14.453
Sorry. Could you put them
in your fridge for me?

00:16:14.536 --> 00:16:17.498
-What did you say?
-My fridge is full.

00:16:17.581 --> 00:16:19.458
They're perishable,
so refrigerate them now.

00:16:19.541 --> 00:16:21.752
-I'm busy. I've got to go.
-Hey, wait…

00:16:28.008 --> 00:16:31.220
I knew you and Officer Song were
childhood friends, but this is unique.

00:16:32.096 --> 00:16:33.847
Did your father really build it?

00:16:33.931 --> 00:16:34.890
Yes.

00:16:34.973 --> 00:16:38.727
So you're basically living together,
but separately.

00:16:39.561 --> 00:16:41.396
You're living together, but not together.

00:16:42.189 --> 00:16:45.025
-Right?
-As an architect…

00:16:45.109 --> 00:16:46.485
I want to see her house too.

00:16:47.778 --> 00:16:49.738
But she won't be happy about it, right?

00:16:49.822 --> 00:16:53.200
The director said
never cross this yellow line.

00:16:57.955 --> 00:17:00.165
-Pizza delivery.
-I didn't order any.

00:17:01.917 --> 00:17:04.503
-That's me.
-Oh, it was here.

00:17:04.586 --> 00:17:05.712
-Yes.
-Enjoy.

00:17:05.796 --> 00:17:06.713
-Thank you.
-Sure.

00:17:10.884 --> 00:17:12.594
Want a piece? You can come over.

00:17:14.054 --> 00:17:15.347
You go ahead and eat.

00:17:23.272 --> 00:17:26.233
Ha-gyeong! Ha-gyeong!

00:17:26.316 --> 00:17:28.944
I made your favorite kimchi pancakes.

00:17:30.445 --> 00:17:31.697
You can't cross that line.

00:17:31.780 --> 00:17:34.992
My guests can only go
as far as this couch here.

00:17:38.412 --> 00:17:40.455
Of course,
you have a ceasefire line at home.

00:17:40.539 --> 00:17:43.041
You live in the DMZ.

00:17:49.381 --> 00:17:50.340
Where…

00:17:54.386 --> 00:17:55.470
What is happening?

00:17:55.554 --> 00:17:56.597
Come in.

00:18:04.605 --> 00:18:06.273
Jeez.

00:18:07.274 --> 00:18:08.525
Let's sit.

00:18:10.319 --> 00:18:14.114
Happy now?
Now I'm invited by both of you.

00:18:14.198 --> 00:18:17.034
Sit and eat now. It'll get cold.

00:18:25.334 --> 00:18:26.543
Here.

00:18:29.546 --> 00:18:32.799
I didn't think of that way.
You're really smart.

00:18:32.883 --> 00:18:36.011
I used my brain. Thanks to Ha-gyeong,
it's smarter now.

00:18:36.637 --> 00:18:40.265
She's so smart and capable.
I should call her "Dr. Song."

00:18:40.933 --> 00:18:43.143
She tutored my daughter
and sent her to college.

00:18:43.227 --> 00:18:45.687
And Jang's immature son
became a decent man

00:18:45.771 --> 00:18:48.815
all thanks to her.
She's an amazing girl.

00:18:48.899 --> 00:18:52.194
I wouldn't trade Dr. Song
for a hundred other doctors.

00:18:52.277 --> 00:18:53.278
Enough. Now, food.

00:19:15.926 --> 00:19:16.927
Again?

00:19:23.850 --> 00:19:25.602
Su-bak, come here.

00:19:25.686 --> 00:19:27.354
How was your day? Have you eaten yet?

00:19:29.523 --> 00:19:30.983
Song! You're home!

00:19:31.733 --> 00:19:32.818
What are you doing here?

00:19:36.405 --> 00:19:37.364
She's here.

00:19:52.587 --> 00:19:55.173
You know what this house means
to Song Ha-gyeong.

00:19:55.257 --> 00:19:56.425
Why are you doing this?

00:19:59.094 --> 00:20:01.263
Your slices are inconsistently cut.

00:20:02.264 --> 00:20:03.682
Do you want me to change knives?

00:20:05.726 --> 00:20:07.978
What's your real reason
for barging into this house?

00:20:09.730 --> 00:20:12.858
I'm just trying to live with
Song Ha-gyeong, who's still growing.

00:20:14.067 --> 00:20:17.154
For now, matching her pace.
Just like this.

00:20:18.155 --> 00:20:19.072
Slowly.

00:20:22.367 --> 00:20:24.369
I had fixed everything for Mom,

00:20:24.453 --> 00:20:26.538
so you won't have any problems
moving around.

00:20:28.915 --> 00:20:30.876
Hey, that aside,

00:20:30.959 --> 00:20:34.880
what on earth did Baek Do-ha do
to make you let him live here?

00:20:34.963 --> 00:20:37.299
-Well…
-He begged.

00:20:39.801 --> 00:20:43.180
We'll live together until August 31,
and if she still doesn't like it,

00:20:44.181 --> 00:20:45.557
I said I'd disappear forever.

00:20:45.640 --> 00:20:47.768
Your last card was strong.

00:20:48.477 --> 00:20:50.854
-Look at this.
-What's this?

00:20:51.646 --> 00:20:53.690
"Detailed contract."

00:20:53.774 --> 00:20:56.068
Is this how you two live together?

00:20:56.151 --> 00:20:59.529
Looking at you both,
you're equally immature.

00:20:59.613 --> 00:21:01.573
-Don't look.
-Hey!

00:21:05.535 --> 00:21:08.246
Hey, this detailed contract

00:21:08.330 --> 00:21:11.750
was all made by Song Ha-gyeong.
It'll be hard living with her, right?

00:21:13.460 --> 00:21:15.379
-Hey.
-Hey, Baek Do.

00:21:15.462 --> 00:21:17.172
You always make me do everything.

00:21:17.255 --> 00:21:18.715
You keep moving around.

00:21:19.841 --> 00:21:20.759
Come on back.

00:21:21.802 --> 00:21:23.678
-Go, hurry up.
-I'm coming.

00:21:24.513 --> 00:21:27.808
She's only harsh to me, isn't she?

00:21:36.149 --> 00:21:37.943
-It's good.
-Right?

00:21:38.026 --> 00:21:38.902
It's really good.

00:21:38.985 --> 00:21:42.197
You just sliced it. I did everything.
I did almost all the plating too.

00:21:42.280 --> 00:21:44.991
I seasoned it. Don't be ridiculous.

00:21:45.075 --> 00:21:46.076
I did everything.

00:21:46.159 --> 00:21:48.620
Slicing and seasoning is
everything in cooking.

00:21:48.703 --> 00:21:50.247
You were so bad at slicing, though.

00:21:50.330 --> 00:21:51.164
It's delicious.

00:21:51.248 --> 00:21:53.208
It's fine, as long as it tastes good.

00:21:53.291 --> 00:21:56.253
-Right?
-Yes, it tastes good.

00:21:56.336 --> 00:21:57.170
See?

00:21:58.296 --> 00:22:00.590
-All right. I'll close the door.
-Thanks.

00:22:12.561 --> 00:22:14.563
Is this why you're living with Baek Do-ha?

00:22:19.234 --> 00:22:21.945
The Peanut House has changed so much
in just a few days.

00:22:24.865 --> 00:22:26.158
It finally feels like a home.

00:22:32.414 --> 00:22:34.416
JONG-MAN JR

00:22:48.847 --> 00:22:50.849
-Thanks for the food! Bye!
-Bye!

00:22:50.932 --> 00:22:52.392
Bye. Thanks for the food.

00:22:52.475 --> 00:22:53.768
Bye!

00:23:02.944 --> 00:23:05.947
Let's go, Su-bak. Come on.

00:23:09.034 --> 00:23:11.411
It's really weird
that they're living together.

00:23:12.120 --> 00:23:14.539
Ha-gyeong seemed happy though, right?

00:23:15.040 --> 00:23:18.960
Yes, it's been a while
since I've seen her smile so genuinely.

00:23:19.586 --> 00:23:22.589
I'll wait until August 31st too,

00:23:23.131 --> 00:23:25.926
but if he makes Song suffer even a bit,
I won't let it slide.

00:23:27.177 --> 00:23:29.930
By the way, Seul, I think I won again.

00:23:30.013 --> 00:23:32.307
I said Song Ha-gyeong
would accept Baek Do-ha.

00:23:33.266 --> 00:23:35.060
Seriously, Song Ha-gyeong.

00:23:35.143 --> 00:23:37.812
She seems really strong,
but she always cuts him some slack.

00:23:40.649 --> 00:23:42.484
-I deposited it.
-Nice.

00:23:47.822 --> 00:23:49.449
By the way,

00:23:49.532 --> 00:23:52.327
I was surprised to hear
you wanted to go to the Peanut House.

00:23:52.410 --> 00:23:55.997
You never go to other peoples' homes,
no matter how close you are.

00:23:56.998 --> 00:23:59.084
Do-ha invited me for the first time.

00:24:00.168 --> 00:24:02.128
So I tried something I don't usually do.

00:24:03.129 --> 00:24:04.130
And also,

00:24:04.673 --> 00:24:07.050
how much longer
can we meet like this?

00:24:20.397 --> 00:24:22.190
Why aren't you saying anything?

00:24:22.274 --> 00:24:24.943
It's about time you said something mean.

00:24:25.777 --> 00:24:28.822
Why say anything?
You'll do whatever you want anyway.

00:24:31.533 --> 00:24:34.995
Still, inviting Seung-taek
was a good thing.

00:24:37.998 --> 00:24:39.874
First praise from Song Ha-gyeong.

00:24:46.965 --> 00:24:49.676
And all you want to do with me
is just eat meals together?

00:24:49.759 --> 00:24:51.303
To cook for me and feed me?

00:24:52.846 --> 00:24:53.972
Why is that "just"?

00:24:55.140 --> 00:24:56.433
That's huge.

00:24:57.892 --> 00:24:59.394
Three meals a day.

00:25:00.145 --> 00:25:03.690
Sounds of spoons, chopsticks,
chewing, and talking.

00:25:04.357 --> 00:25:05.775
These are so precious.

00:25:08.403 --> 00:25:10.238
I want you to think of me…

00:25:10.989 --> 00:25:12.449
every time you eat.

00:25:14.576 --> 00:25:15.535
Actually,

00:25:16.536 --> 00:25:19.122
I want to make you think of me
in every corner of the house.

00:25:20.540 --> 00:25:23.126
Eating together, sleeping together,

00:25:23.209 --> 00:25:26.004
working together,
and inviting people we both know,

00:25:27.005 --> 00:25:28.840
I want you to think of me always.

00:25:46.775 --> 00:25:48.401
It finally feels like a home.

00:26:26.439 --> 00:26:27.732
Can't sleep?

00:26:29.484 --> 00:26:30.693
No.

00:26:31.694 --> 00:26:33.154
Right.

00:26:33.238 --> 00:26:36.074
I can't sleep,
so I'm trying to read this book.

00:26:40.912 --> 00:26:43.373
The sleep kit I bought doesn't work?

00:26:49.170 --> 00:26:51.005
If that worked,

00:26:51.089 --> 00:26:53.716
I wouldn't be going
to the sleep clinic I can barely afford.

00:26:53.800 --> 00:26:56.761
And in this house,
all the deer sounds and training noises

00:26:56.845 --> 00:26:58.972
wake me up in the middle of the night.

00:27:01.474 --> 00:27:02.600
You must've been scared.

00:27:04.811 --> 00:27:08.690
Don't be ridiculous.
It's not scary. I'm a grown-up woman.

00:27:12.569 --> 00:27:13.987
By the way,

00:27:14.070 --> 00:27:17.824
did you contact the lawyer
about postponing the mediation?

00:27:23.455 --> 00:27:25.832
Right. Did you watch that drama yesterday?

00:27:26.624 --> 00:27:29.419
-I didn't.
-That famous one.

00:27:29.502 --> 00:27:30.336
Right.

00:27:30.420 --> 00:27:32.464
-It's so good these days.
-It is.

00:27:32.547 --> 00:27:35.800
I want you to think of me
every time you eat.

00:27:35.884 --> 00:27:36.968
You aren't eating much.

00:27:39.345 --> 00:27:40.263
It's nothing.

00:27:42.182 --> 00:27:44.184
It tastes a bit different
from what I know.

00:27:45.935 --> 00:27:47.479
-Who is it?
-Hello.

00:27:48.521 --> 00:27:50.315
-I'll tell you if it goes well.
-Honey.

00:27:50.398 --> 00:27:51.608
-Yes?
-Are you okay?

00:27:51.691 --> 00:27:53.359
-What do you mean?
-Look at this.

00:27:54.152 --> 00:27:55.737
PACHEON CITY HALL BULLETIN BOARD

00:27:57.322 --> 00:27:58.698
JEON NAM-JIN
STATUS: RETURN

00:27:59.365 --> 00:28:01.618
Excuse me. Sorry.

00:28:05.538 --> 00:28:06.915
JEON NAM-JIN

00:28:10.043 --> 00:28:10.960
Darn it.

00:28:11.044 --> 00:28:11.878
Cheers!

00:28:11.961 --> 00:28:13.505
-Patan!
-Patan!

00:28:14.964 --> 00:28:15.798
Cheers!

00:28:18.843 --> 00:28:20.220
How much is that project?

00:28:20.845 --> 00:28:22.013
Budget's 12 billion won.

00:28:23.181 --> 00:28:26.518
The mayor picked this project
for re-election.

00:28:26.601 --> 00:28:30.271
I heard it was finally rejected,
but they're doing it.

00:28:30.939 --> 00:28:33.399
So who won it?

00:28:33.483 --> 00:28:35.401
Someone has better ties than Nam-jin?

00:28:35.485 --> 00:28:36.694
-Would there be?
-No.

00:28:36.778 --> 00:28:40.406
If you win public support
with public architecture,

00:28:40.490 --> 00:28:44.327
you can go straight to City Council,
and even become a governor and a mayor.

00:28:44.410 --> 00:28:46.955
-Hello.
-I have a reservation at 7:00.

00:28:47.956 --> 00:28:49.332
It's the innermost room.

00:28:54.838 --> 00:28:57.382
Hey, who's this?

00:28:57.465 --> 00:29:00.385
Lawyer Seo, funny we meet here.

00:29:02.679 --> 00:29:04.138
It's really so good to see you.

00:29:05.223 --> 00:29:06.474
Wait. Hold on.

00:29:07.350 --> 00:29:08.518
Are you here to see me?

00:29:09.811 --> 00:29:10.728
Come here.

00:29:11.271 --> 00:29:13.273
Hey, guys, say hello.

00:29:13.356 --> 00:29:16.359
This is Lawyer Seo from Seo & Joo.

00:29:18.528 --> 00:29:19.362
Hello.

00:29:19.445 --> 00:29:23.241
He only works
for first-class VIPs like me.

00:29:23.324 --> 00:29:24.367
Applause.

00:29:25.451 --> 00:29:28.079
-Seo & Joo!
-Seo & Joo!

00:29:28.162 --> 00:29:30.290
-Seo & Joo! Seo and…
-Seo & Joo! Seo and…

00:29:30.957 --> 00:29:33.293
My party is waiting. Excuse me.

00:29:34.168 --> 00:29:35.295
Okay.

00:29:45.013 --> 00:29:46.222
You're here.

00:29:46.764 --> 00:29:48.975
You're the lawyer
who only works for VIPs.

00:29:49.058 --> 00:29:50.727
The soundproofing is terrible.

00:29:53.062 --> 00:29:56.441
Thanks to that, I became a VIP too.

00:30:02.989 --> 00:30:06.409
Postponing mediation
isn't difficult at all…

00:30:07.577 --> 00:30:10.580
but I'm curious how you two
suddenly came to live together.

00:30:11.539 --> 00:30:12.790
I'd like to learn the skill.

00:30:14.918 --> 00:30:17.170
What skill?

00:30:18.212 --> 00:30:22.258
Ms. Song Ha-gyeong was quite stubborn

00:30:22.342 --> 00:30:24.260
when playing bingo with me.

00:30:26.554 --> 00:30:27.722
Bingo game?

00:30:28.765 --> 00:30:31.392
You two met up alone?

00:30:31.976 --> 00:30:32.936
Yes.

00:30:33.645 --> 00:30:37.398
I find Plaintiff Song Ha-gyeong
more and more interesting.

00:30:39.275 --> 00:30:42.570
Right. She's not easy to deal with.

00:30:44.280 --> 00:30:46.282
Wait. Hold on a second.

00:30:49.494 --> 00:30:50.453
Yes?

00:30:50.536 --> 00:30:53.665
Of course.
The materials and the construction

00:30:53.748 --> 00:30:57.502
should all involve us locals.
What are you talking about?

00:30:58.503 --> 00:31:01.589
I don't know.
Let's meet soon and talk, okay?

00:31:17.271 --> 00:31:19.565
I heard
you're going to be joining our project.

00:31:21.150 --> 00:31:24.612
As a public architect,
you'll advise us and manage the site.

00:31:24.696 --> 00:31:25.613
Yes.

00:31:26.280 --> 00:31:28.992
Right. I was rude last time.

00:31:31.995 --> 00:31:37.291
Coming from abroad,
you wouldn't know the local context.

00:31:37.375 --> 00:31:38.960
Given local context,

00:31:39.043 --> 00:31:41.295
I know well
we should work with a local architect.

00:31:42.422 --> 00:31:44.173
I look forward to working with you.

00:31:45.299 --> 00:31:46.300
Right. I…

00:31:47.552 --> 00:31:50.430
What? Okay.

00:31:51.139 --> 00:31:52.181
Nice.

00:31:52.682 --> 00:31:53.683
You got this.

00:32:04.318 --> 00:32:05.445
Right.

00:32:07.030 --> 00:32:09.198
First of all…

00:32:10.658 --> 00:32:11.868
Jeez, my chest is burning.

00:32:11.951 --> 00:32:14.328
First, Director Baek should know

00:32:15.246 --> 00:32:17.540
that the
Public Architecture Department's opinion

00:32:17.623 --> 00:32:19.167
is the city's opinion.

00:32:20.251 --> 00:32:21.919
One thousand of Suhyeon-ri residents

00:32:22.003 --> 00:32:24.047
and 13,000 Patan-myeon residents

00:32:24.130 --> 00:32:26.340
and 170,000 Patan City residents.

00:32:26.424 --> 00:32:27.425
It represents them all.

00:32:27.508 --> 00:32:28.926
That freak…

00:32:34.682 --> 00:32:38.019
Baek Do-ha's going to lash out
at Jeon Nam-jin for cutting his tree.

00:32:41.147 --> 00:32:42.815
Please cover for my shortcomings.

00:32:42.899 --> 00:32:45.651
I'm excited to work with someone
with a deep understanding

00:32:45.735 --> 00:32:47.528
of the local context.

00:32:47.612 --> 00:32:49.280
-What?
-Architecture…

00:32:49.363 --> 00:32:51.407
is all about locality.

00:32:51.491 --> 00:32:53.201
And on-site, just trust me…

00:32:53.284 --> 00:32:56.287
He's totally professionally
ignoring him.

00:32:56.370 --> 00:32:59.957
I've been having my eye on
the warehouse renovation project

00:33:00.041 --> 00:33:02.043
that the former director did too.

00:33:02.126 --> 00:33:04.170
-Why is he like that?
-Oh, my.

00:33:04.253 --> 00:33:08.424
That was also done with Officer Song here.
We were working together.

00:33:13.387 --> 00:33:14.639
Let's wrap it up here today.

00:33:15.515 --> 00:33:17.683
You two figure out your rhythm gradually.

00:33:20.812 --> 00:33:21.646
All right.

00:33:38.079 --> 00:33:41.165
In case you hear something weird

00:33:41.749 --> 00:33:45.044
and misunderstand and misinterpret it
while working at the City Hall,

00:33:45.128 --> 00:33:46.212
I'll tell you first.

00:33:47.713 --> 00:33:49.298
I once sued someone over Jong-man.

00:33:51.384 --> 00:33:55.763
Jeon Nam-jin was involved in it.
I don't want to get into the details.

00:33:56.973 --> 00:33:59.517
Anyway, something like that happened,

00:33:59.600 --> 00:34:03.437
and I won the lawsuit,
and he was fined seven million won.

00:34:03.521 --> 00:34:04.438
That happened once.

00:34:06.774 --> 00:34:08.734
It was resolved peacefully,

00:34:08.818 --> 00:34:12.780
so don't bring personal feelings
into professional work either.

00:34:15.658 --> 00:34:18.369
It doesn't seem resolved at all.

00:34:18.452 --> 00:34:21.289
Tell me more details.

00:34:21.372 --> 00:34:23.916
Don't ask anymore.
My trauma's coming back.

00:34:24.500 --> 00:34:26.669
So did you really date Jeon Nam-jin?

00:34:28.796 --> 00:34:30.339
Why do you want to know that now?

00:34:32.091 --> 00:34:32.967
It's because of you!

00:34:33.926 --> 00:34:37.555
It's because of you,
so don't ask me anymore, okay?

00:34:38.472 --> 00:34:39.640
It's all because of you!

00:34:40.474 --> 00:34:42.727
Today's bad air quality
is because of you,

00:34:42.810 --> 00:34:45.396
him only pooping once today
is because of you,

00:34:45.479 --> 00:34:48.065
and what I hate the most,
tangsuyuk with sauce poured on it…

00:34:48.149 --> 00:34:49.483
That's all because of you too!

00:34:56.824 --> 00:34:58.784
Are you sure you have time for this?

00:34:58.868 --> 00:35:01.204
Are you prepared for tomorrow's meeting?

00:35:01.287 --> 00:35:02.788
The hazing on the site is no joke.

00:35:02.872 --> 00:35:05.249
Don't grovel on-site
and embarrass me, okay?

00:35:09.086 --> 00:35:10.588
What's wrong with her?

00:35:13.049 --> 00:35:16.636
Su-bak.
You only pooped once today?

00:35:16.719 --> 00:35:17.803
OBSERVATORY RENOVATION

00:35:17.887 --> 00:35:20.264
Thank you for your hard work.

00:35:20.348 --> 00:35:23.267
Hello, yes. Hello.

00:35:23.351 --> 00:35:24.352
Hello.

00:35:24.435 --> 00:35:26.646
-Thank you for your hard work.
-Oh, my.

00:35:26.729 --> 00:35:29.815
Hey, bro! We meet on this site too.

00:35:29.899 --> 00:35:30.900
You look great.

00:35:30.983 --> 00:35:32.485
Come on.

00:35:32.568 --> 00:35:35.696
Why aren't you coming
to the morning soccer club anymore?

00:35:36.489 --> 00:35:39.533
Seeing Director Jeon Nam-jin
puts my mind at ease.

00:35:39.617 --> 00:35:42.536
The blueprint for this project
really worried me.

00:35:42.620 --> 00:35:45.122
It's such a creative blueprint.

00:35:45.206 --> 00:35:48.209
It's even specifying machines by area.

00:35:48.834 --> 00:35:51.879
I've never seen something like that
in 30 years of my carpentry career.

00:35:51.963 --> 00:35:53.839
Where's he from?

00:35:53.923 --> 00:35:55.383
He doesn't seem local.

00:35:55.466 --> 00:35:57.176
He's…

00:35:57.260 --> 00:36:00.554
He grew up in New York with his mother,
who's an architecture professor.

00:36:00.638 --> 00:36:03.891
Public architecture is hard for outsiders.

00:36:03.975 --> 00:36:06.519
That's why I'm attached.

00:36:06.602 --> 00:36:11.315
No wonder. He's clearly someone
who just draws plans at a desk.

00:36:11.399 --> 00:36:14.568
Last time, I was even told
to break the bearing wall.

00:36:14.652 --> 00:36:16.070
I was totally dumbfounded.

00:36:16.612 --> 00:36:20.116
I'll listen to your advice and skip it.
Let's just do it that way.

00:36:20.199 --> 00:36:22.743
Bro, just trust me.

00:36:22.827 --> 00:36:25.454
Without my advice,
you can't meet the deadline.

00:36:25.538 --> 00:36:26.622
And today…

00:36:26.706 --> 00:36:29.333
Director Baek, where are you?

00:36:29.417 --> 00:36:30.501
Everyone's here--

00:36:31.544 --> 00:36:32.378
What?

00:36:35.339 --> 00:36:38.134
Director Baek,
you're supposed to be in the office now.

00:36:38.217 --> 00:36:39.385
This…

00:36:40.553 --> 00:36:41.846
Why's this wall standing?

00:36:43.806 --> 00:36:45.057
It's a load-bearing wall.

00:36:45.766 --> 00:36:49.353
If you just break it,
the building will collapse.

00:36:53.816 --> 00:36:55.943
I marked non-bearing walls for demolition.

00:36:57.486 --> 00:36:58.821
Did you not see the blueprint?

00:37:07.663 --> 00:37:09.582
Gosh, seriously!

00:37:09.665 --> 00:37:11.959
That's your blueprint.

00:37:12.043 --> 00:37:15.629
Patan High School is old,
and has no original plans. Right?

00:37:18.132 --> 00:37:20.176
Come out.

00:37:22.136 --> 00:37:23.220
Look.

00:37:27.016 --> 00:37:28.642
You hear this sound?

00:37:28.726 --> 00:37:31.062
Load-bearing and non-load-bearing

00:37:31.145 --> 00:37:34.440
have different densities,
so the sound is subtly different.

00:37:35.566 --> 00:37:38.110
It might be too difficult for you.

00:37:39.445 --> 00:37:40.363
What the…

00:37:44.158 --> 00:37:45.534
Do you think the same, sir?

00:37:46.243 --> 00:37:48.829
He's right. They're all connected.

00:37:49.622 --> 00:37:52.833
You've only been in the office.
You don't know the site.

00:37:54.794 --> 00:37:57.088
All right, guys.

00:37:58.589 --> 00:38:00.383
Today we're…

00:38:00.466 --> 00:38:04.220
This is the last day.
Let's not waste energy. It's a good day.

00:38:04.303 --> 00:38:07.431
Should we do it
on the beam and the column now?

00:38:07.515 --> 00:38:09.141
Would that satisfy him?

00:38:09.225 --> 00:38:11.977
Then we'll have to remove
the ceiling and walls too.

00:38:12.645 --> 00:38:14.939
Are all the walls removed yet?

00:38:15.648 --> 00:38:18.776
Just break everything
as he says with a breaker.

00:38:18.859 --> 00:38:20.152
Then the site will be ruined.

00:38:21.320 --> 00:38:24.698
Everyone go to the office first.
You can talk there…

00:38:33.165 --> 00:38:33.999
What are you doing?

00:38:34.875 --> 00:38:35.960
Are you crazy?

00:38:38.295 --> 00:38:40.214
Wait. Don't.

00:38:48.222 --> 00:38:49.723
What? Don't!

00:38:51.058 --> 00:38:52.393
Please don't!

00:38:55.521 --> 00:38:56.730
Don't, please!

00:39:09.034 --> 00:39:11.579
Should I break that one too?

00:39:12.913 --> 00:39:15.124
I'll finish it.

00:39:22.006 --> 00:39:25.217
Sir, I need you to trust…

00:39:27.636 --> 00:39:28.846
my blueprint.

00:39:31.432 --> 00:39:32.266
Okay.

00:39:33.934 --> 00:39:36.395
I checked the level with a tape

00:39:36.479 --> 00:39:38.647
and measured it for over a month.

00:39:39.899 --> 00:39:40.983
I heard that

00:39:42.109 --> 00:39:45.404
you're finishing up today.
Shouldn't you move quickly?

00:39:46.030 --> 00:39:48.115
As you know, our schedule is tight.

00:39:48.199 --> 00:39:50.910
But if we have defect,
it'll be a big trouble.

00:40:10.054 --> 00:40:12.973
Why did I avoid his eyes earlier?

00:40:19.939 --> 00:40:21.982
This isn't the Baek Do-ha I knew.

00:40:23.651 --> 00:40:26.570
I probably didn't know much about him.

00:40:28.239 --> 00:40:32.159
He only stayed for 21 days,
and then flew back before summer ended.

00:40:32.826 --> 00:40:34.662
Of course I didn't know him.

00:40:55.474 --> 00:40:56.433
Whatever.

00:41:05.484 --> 00:41:06.652
It's just a black goat.

00:41:06.735 --> 00:41:09.154
Why did you come down
to the humans' territory?

00:41:18.831 --> 00:41:19.665
Chang-su?

00:41:22.084 --> 00:41:23.210
Gosh, you scared me.

00:41:24.253 --> 00:41:26.297
What brings you here?

00:41:26.380 --> 00:41:29.258
Is someone else living here now?

00:41:31.760 --> 00:41:34.555
Mr. Baek's son is staying for a bit.

00:41:36.849 --> 00:41:37.850
I see.

00:41:38.559 --> 00:41:39.518
Why do you ask?

00:41:43.731 --> 00:41:44.565
What the…

00:42:03.751 --> 00:42:04.918
What was that?

00:42:12.509 --> 00:42:14.303
What's going on?

00:42:25.564 --> 00:42:28.025
Jeez, not again!

00:42:36.617 --> 00:42:38.452
-Hello.
-Baek Do-ha, where are you?

00:42:38.535 --> 00:42:41.580
I'm trapped at home.
The door won't open.

00:42:41.664 --> 00:42:42.956
Where are you?

00:42:43.040 --> 00:42:45.918
-The bathroom.
-Okay. I'll be right there.

00:42:47.920 --> 00:42:49.546
-Song Ha-gyeong.
-You came?

00:42:49.630 --> 00:42:51.256
I'm here. Move away from the door.

00:42:53.967 --> 00:42:55.177
Jeez.

00:42:59.473 --> 00:43:00.599
Thanks.

00:43:17.074 --> 00:43:20.828
Maybe I should really move out
of this crappy house. The location's bad.

00:43:21.704 --> 00:43:23.372
Why did Dad build a wooden house

00:43:23.455 --> 00:43:25.541
that creaks and cracks
whenever it rains?

00:43:26.125 --> 00:43:28.836
Right. I saw a black goat
in front of the house today.

00:43:28.919 --> 00:43:31.755
You should've called me sooner.

00:43:31.839 --> 00:43:34.800
Don't underestimate this house.

00:43:39.888 --> 00:43:40.723
Right.

00:43:42.057 --> 00:43:43.434
I should tell you this now…

00:43:45.060 --> 00:43:46.687
since you're living here for a while.

00:44:03.245 --> 00:44:05.247
Sometimes, lights were on
in an empty room.

00:44:08.959 --> 00:44:10.210
Is this happening again?

00:44:28.061 --> 00:44:30.063
Some doors fixed themselves.

00:44:32.983 --> 00:44:34.777
What's wrong with this thing?

00:44:41.909 --> 00:44:44.286
A broken faucet
suddenly started working perfectly.

00:44:48.540 --> 00:44:49.625
MASTER BAEK

00:44:52.961 --> 00:44:55.214
-Hey, Ha-gyeong.
-Hi, Mr. Baek.

00:44:55.297 --> 00:44:56.673
Did you come to my house?

00:44:56.757 --> 00:45:00.219
What? No, I haven't been yet.

00:45:00.302 --> 00:45:02.137
I'll definitely come this week.

00:45:03.805 --> 00:45:05.891
Maybe there's a ghost in this house.

00:45:05.974 --> 00:45:08.143
-So don't--
-I fixed it.

00:45:10.229 --> 00:45:13.482
I'm talking about things
that happened before you came.

00:45:13.565 --> 00:45:15.901
-One year ago--
-I know. I fixed it.

00:45:19.404 --> 00:45:23.075
What? Really?
You've been sneaking into my house?

00:45:23.617 --> 00:45:26.078
How could a ghost have fixed
all those things here?

00:45:26.161 --> 00:45:28.413
-Grow up.
-Hey.

00:45:28.497 --> 00:45:32.543
Every time you asked my dad for help,
he told me to come here.

00:45:33.043 --> 00:45:36.755
I knew you'd freak out if you saw me,
so I came when you were away.

00:45:38.382 --> 00:45:39.841
You told me to disappear.

00:45:39.925 --> 00:45:43.303
So to avoid upsetting you,
I came while you were away for work.

00:45:46.723 --> 00:45:47.766
Song Ha-gyeong.

00:45:59.152 --> 00:46:02.823
A ghost? You have a serious problem.

00:46:12.374 --> 00:46:14.293
If anything needs fixing, call me.

00:46:28.890 --> 00:46:30.183
Jeez, you scared me.

00:46:31.560 --> 00:46:33.854
Hey, I just checked.

00:46:33.937 --> 00:46:36.231
You know the hallway
from the lobby to the office.

00:46:36.315 --> 00:46:38.025
There'll be a structure going in.

00:46:38.108 --> 00:46:39.443
So that line might go over.

00:46:43.363 --> 00:46:45.032
SHARED SPACE
PLEASE TAKE CALLS OUTSIDE

00:46:45.657 --> 00:46:47.909
Hey, I'll call you back.

00:46:50.829 --> 00:46:53.081
Let's go. You must be feeling great.

00:46:59.755 --> 00:47:00.589
Let's go.

00:47:01.340 --> 00:47:02.507
Let's go.

00:47:02.591 --> 00:47:05.761
-Rub him properly.
-I am doing that.

00:47:09.139 --> 00:47:10.891
Good boy.

00:47:11.350 --> 00:47:12.934
You're being such a good boy today.

00:47:15.145 --> 00:47:16.855
-Chairwoman.
-Hi.

00:47:17.356 --> 00:47:18.190
Hello.

00:47:19.524 --> 00:47:20.692
Oh, hello.

00:47:30.118 --> 00:47:31.036
Here I go.

00:47:37.209 --> 00:47:38.335
You've been holding that?

00:47:39.211 --> 00:47:40.045
Oh, please.

00:47:44.049 --> 00:47:46.301
Hey, give it.

00:47:46.385 --> 00:47:48.178
Take this.

00:48:11.201 --> 00:48:12.661
-Hey.
-Did you eat the gimbap?

00:48:12.744 --> 00:48:13.912
I'm eating it now.

00:48:13.995 --> 00:48:15.789
I made a smoothie too.

00:48:15.872 --> 00:48:17.332
I'm drinking that too.

00:48:18.250 --> 00:48:19.459
Enjoy.

00:48:21.086 --> 00:48:23.004
I will. Thanks.

00:48:59.249 --> 00:49:00.292
Yes, coming.

00:49:08.800 --> 00:49:09.926
Who are you?

00:49:11.720 --> 00:49:12.971
Baek Do-ha's house?

00:49:16.224 --> 00:49:17.225
Next door.

00:49:30.655 --> 00:49:32.574
It's scary how fast you move.

00:49:32.657 --> 00:49:34.701
You received my mail less than a day ago.

00:49:34.785 --> 00:49:38.163
Right after the conference,
I heard about you and took a late flight.

00:49:38.246 --> 00:49:40.665
The fastest time slot
was only business class,

00:49:40.749 --> 00:49:42.542
so my month's rent's gone.

00:49:42.626 --> 00:49:44.002
That must've hurt you.

00:49:44.085 --> 00:49:47.839
You suddenly quit your job
and went to Korea. That was fine.

00:49:48.340 --> 00:49:50.926
At least you've been working
remotely on video calls.

00:49:51.635 --> 00:49:54.471
That was fine too.
At first, it was video calls.

00:49:54.554 --> 00:49:55.764
Then it was emails.

00:49:56.306 --> 00:49:57.766
Then you said you wanted to quit.

00:49:57.849 --> 00:50:00.560
I have a project to focus on.

00:50:00.644 --> 00:50:02.479
Are you really ditching Hermann Project?

00:50:02.938 --> 00:50:03.855
It's your design.

00:50:06.024 --> 00:50:09.152
The whole flight here,
I racked my brain.

00:50:11.738 --> 00:50:13.281
"It must be Baek Do-young.

00:50:14.282 --> 00:50:17.327
Okay, I'll somehow persuade him.

00:50:18.370 --> 00:50:20.622
I'll drag him back
even if I have to beat him."

00:50:22.624 --> 00:50:24.042
Is it because of Song Ha-gyeong?

00:50:26.378 --> 00:50:29.005
-Living together.
-Working together too.

00:50:30.382 --> 00:50:32.551
You're doing something
you usually don't do.

00:50:33.176 --> 00:50:36.847
You must be that desperate
and staking everything on it.

00:50:36.930 --> 00:50:39.349
Bringing personal matters
into professional work?

00:50:40.767 --> 00:50:43.061
You don't know Officer Song well.

00:50:43.854 --> 00:50:44.855
She's competent.

00:50:45.939 --> 00:50:47.232
She's the best at her job.

00:50:49.985 --> 00:50:51.152
I'll leave for now.

00:50:52.445 --> 00:50:54.447
I need to revise my strategy too.

00:51:01.496 --> 00:51:03.498
So did you explain everything?

00:51:05.417 --> 00:51:08.253
You came to explain everything. Did you?

00:51:10.005 --> 00:51:11.882
You couldn't sleep even with pills.

00:51:12.507 --> 00:51:14.593
The reason why I've been bothering you.

00:51:16.386 --> 00:51:19.556
The reason
why I had to fly here to this house.

00:51:21.099 --> 00:51:22.309
Did you explain it all?

00:51:26.396 --> 00:51:29.691
I really need to take you back.

00:51:30.984 --> 00:51:32.152
I'll leave for now.

00:52:02.098 --> 00:52:03.350
Hey.

00:52:03.975 --> 00:52:06.436
That woman who made
a spectacular entrance earlier

00:52:06.519 --> 00:52:08.647
is someone I studied with in New York--

00:52:08.730 --> 00:52:10.148
Why are you explaining that?

00:52:11.274 --> 00:52:12.734
It's not something unusual.

00:52:16.321 --> 00:52:18.323
Give them the right address, though.

00:52:19.199 --> 00:52:21.117
Why always make them ring my bell?

00:52:24.454 --> 00:52:25.538
Well…

00:52:26.915 --> 00:52:28.083
You have something to say?

00:52:29.084 --> 00:52:30.669
I have work to finish now.

00:52:33.672 --> 00:52:34.798
No, go ahead, work.

00:53:03.243 --> 00:53:04.494
Baek Do-ha's house?

00:53:19.592 --> 00:53:20.719
I'm Yoon So-hee.

00:53:22.095 --> 00:53:23.096
I'm Song Ha-gyeong.

00:53:25.015 --> 00:53:27.017
Friends with Baek Do-ha and Do-young?

00:53:30.145 --> 00:53:31.312
You know Baek Do-young?

00:53:31.396 --> 00:53:33.106
He always came in winter.

00:53:34.399 --> 00:53:38.111
Baek Do-ha's mother was my professor.
Professor Nam Ae-min.

00:53:39.988 --> 00:53:40.822
I see.

00:53:40.905 --> 00:53:43.324
You don't know me well,
but I know you well.

00:53:44.743 --> 00:53:46.995
I heard about you endlessly
from both of them.

00:53:47.787 --> 00:53:51.624
The childhood friend living next door
in the Peanut House in Korea.

00:53:54.586 --> 00:53:56.463
But why did you come to see me?

00:53:57.922 --> 00:53:58.757
Song Ha-gyeong.

00:54:01.426 --> 00:54:02.510
Do you like Baek Do-ha?

00:54:08.933 --> 00:54:11.978
Do you genuinely like him?

00:54:15.148 --> 00:54:16.399
-I--
-I like him.

00:54:19.402 --> 00:54:23.114
But I like Architect Baek Do-ha
twice as much as the man…

00:54:24.157 --> 00:54:25.700
No, ten times more.

00:54:26.743 --> 00:54:30.080
If I had to choose one,
without a moment's hesitation,

00:54:30.163 --> 00:54:31.748
I'd choose Architect Baek Do-ha.

00:54:32.749 --> 00:54:35.335
I love the designs
Baek Do-ha created that much.

00:54:37.420 --> 00:54:38.254
Okay.

00:54:41.257 --> 00:54:43.301
But why are you telling me this?

00:54:49.182 --> 00:54:52.352
You'll live together
until August 31st, right?

00:54:53.394 --> 00:54:57.232
But I want to take Baek Do-ha
right now.

00:55:00.401 --> 00:55:03.947
I want you to let him
go back to where he belongs.

00:55:05.073 --> 00:55:06.157
Please let him go.

00:55:54.747 --> 00:55:58.084
Early on in the project,
we held an internal team competition.

00:55:58.918 --> 00:56:02.255
Baek Do-ha's design was the only one
that got unanimous approval.

00:56:03.256 --> 00:56:05.633
He devoted over two years to it,

00:56:05.717 --> 00:56:07.302
and he's giving it all up…

00:56:08.261 --> 00:56:09.929
to live with you.

00:56:10.597 --> 00:56:13.308
But I'm taking him back within a week.

00:56:14.309 --> 00:56:16.561
It's too important an opportunity for him.

00:56:29.282 --> 00:56:30.533
If he's leaving anyway…

00:56:31.534 --> 00:56:33.369
why did he change that thing?

00:56:35.288 --> 00:56:36.664
My resolutions

00:56:37.290 --> 00:56:39.209
melted away in an instant.

00:56:40.877 --> 00:56:44.756
All those resolutions I froze
melted away.

00:56:45.924 --> 00:56:49.510
Because of the bright lights
that suddenly turned on in this house.

00:56:51.888 --> 00:56:55.642
Don't let anyone in.
Don't get carried away too soon.

00:56:57.227 --> 00:56:59.062
Don't try to trust again.

00:57:03.066 --> 00:57:04.150
Su-bak.

00:57:14.160 --> 00:57:15.203
Su-bak?

00:57:26.130 --> 00:57:26.965
Hey, Su-bak.

00:57:30.760 --> 00:57:31.594
Su-bak.

00:57:32.512 --> 00:57:34.639
Su-bak, wake up. Su-bak.

00:57:38.226 --> 00:57:39.394
Hospital.

00:57:39.477 --> 00:57:40.645
BAEK DO-HA

00:57:51.406 --> 00:57:52.865
The call cannot be connected…

00:57:52.949 --> 00:57:54.158
SONG HA-GYEONG

00:57:59.122 --> 00:58:01.624
Yes, I've turned down the AC.

00:58:02.292 --> 00:58:05.753
And wiping him with a wet towel
lowered his temperature.

00:58:06.337 --> 00:58:08.923
His tongue's a bit swollen
and has no energy yet.

00:58:09.465 --> 00:58:10.758
I'll give him electrolytes.

00:58:12.594 --> 00:58:14.762
Yes, thank you.

00:58:17.181 --> 00:58:19.058
What's wrong? Is Su-bak sick?

00:58:19.726 --> 00:58:23.605
-Should you take him to the hospital?
-It's okay. I've always done this alone.

00:58:26.983 --> 00:58:28.067
You must've been scared.

00:58:35.074 --> 00:58:36.826
Why did you fix the shoe rack?

00:58:38.036 --> 00:58:41.831
That's how Su-bak knows
I'm home from work.

00:58:43.082 --> 00:58:45.835
I didn't leave it broken. It's our signal.

00:58:46.836 --> 00:58:49.380
Your job is designing
and arranging fantasies,

00:58:49.464 --> 00:58:51.591
so you thought
I'd be grateful if you fixed it?

00:58:52.133 --> 00:58:53.009
This is a home.

00:58:54.135 --> 00:58:57.513
Not a blueprint or 3D screen house,
a real home.

00:59:01.976 --> 00:59:03.645
You never lived here, you won't know.

00:59:07.940 --> 00:59:09.192
So don't touch anything.

00:59:18.117 --> 00:59:19.494
Did something happen?

00:59:21.287 --> 00:59:24.540
What happened? It's something
I've always done alone.

00:59:26.459 --> 00:59:30.004
You leaving your traces

00:59:31.089 --> 00:59:32.256
is just ridiculous.

01:00:00.451 --> 01:00:01.786
Just go to your room.

01:00:02.662 --> 01:00:04.372
It's okay. I can do it alone.

01:00:39.866 --> 01:00:41.868
I knew from the beginning.

01:00:42.410 --> 01:00:43.619
Since Baek Do-ha returned

01:00:44.162 --> 01:00:46.539
and the light near my room
turned on again that night.

01:00:48.291 --> 01:00:49.459
My hands…

01:00:50.877 --> 01:00:52.462
would get cold again.

01:00:55.673 --> 01:00:58.301
Girls, stop being picky with food

01:00:58.384 --> 01:01:00.720
and stop going to bed late.
You won't grow tall.

01:01:03.389 --> 01:01:05.016
You little brats!

01:01:05.641 --> 01:01:06.809
Don't ever come back!

01:01:13.524 --> 01:01:15.777
Hurry, please come quickly.

01:01:16.652 --> 01:01:18.488
Please, I'm begging you.

01:01:18.571 --> 01:01:20.823
Mom.

01:01:21.616 --> 01:01:23.618
How can you leave
when Mom's like that?

01:01:23.701 --> 01:01:26.412
Ha-gyeong, I'm not running away.

01:01:26.496 --> 01:01:28.456
-I'm going to go make money.
-You are though.

01:01:28.539 --> 01:01:29.791
No, I'm not.

01:01:30.583 --> 01:01:33.085
Take good care of Mom
until I come back, okay?

01:01:36.964 --> 01:01:37.965
Dad.

01:01:42.553 --> 01:01:43.763
Don't ever come back!

01:01:45.348 --> 01:01:47.558
A house that only shows
people's backs leaving.

01:01:53.773 --> 01:01:55.650
A house that causes insomnia.

01:01:57.276 --> 01:01:58.319
In this house…

01:01:59.403 --> 01:02:01.113
memories of cold hands…

01:02:02.949 --> 01:02:04.283
float around.

01:02:11.165 --> 01:02:12.083
It's okay.

01:02:14.001 --> 01:02:15.461
This house is a place

01:02:16.295 --> 01:02:18.005
where people come and go.

01:02:19.549 --> 01:02:20.550
That's…

01:02:22.093 --> 01:02:23.469
That's the kind of house it is.

01:02:38.776 --> 01:02:39.694
Just…

01:02:43.155 --> 01:02:44.657
You looked so cold.

01:02:49.287 --> 01:02:50.580
And it's summer.

01:02:51.956 --> 01:02:53.040
What do you mean?

01:02:56.794 --> 01:02:57.962
I know.

01:02:59.589 --> 01:03:00.548
That's…

01:03:03.634 --> 01:03:04.927
what you're saying right now.

01:03:52.975 --> 01:03:53.809
Yoon So-hee?

01:03:53.893 --> 01:03:56.437
Architect Baek Do-ha's official partner.

01:03:56.520 --> 01:04:00.524
An architect with skills, looks, speech.
That's not common.

01:04:00.608 --> 01:04:01.776
What can you do about it?

01:04:01.859 --> 01:04:04.195
Would you have done this
if it were So-hee?

01:04:04.278 --> 01:04:06.155
Go where you belong.

01:04:06.238 --> 01:04:09.867
Song Ha-gyeong, do you really want me
to disappear from your life?

01:04:10.743 --> 01:04:12.662
You didn't answer over 20 calls?

01:04:12.745 --> 01:04:14.455
If I don't answer, you should know.

01:04:14.538 --> 01:04:17.166
Why do you become an 18-year-old
when you're with me?

01:04:17.249 --> 01:04:20.044
Don't make that face
like you're about to cry.

01:04:20.127 --> 01:04:21.963
-Are you done talking?
-No.

01:04:22.046 --> 01:04:25.257
There's more.
I'm so embarrassed because of you!

01:04:26.842 --> 01:04:27.969
Did you come to tease me?

01:04:28.511 --> 01:04:31.472
I think I have feelings for you.

01:04:31.555 --> 01:04:32.765
Let's date.